{:edb/db-before-t 1856 :edb/db-after-t 1857 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535169 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:32:14.271Z" 13194139535169 true] [17592186124402 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335171 13194139535169 true] [17592186124402 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335192 13194139535169 true] [17592186124510 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335178 13194139535169 true] [17592186124510 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335199 13194139535169 true] [17592186124549 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335185 13194139535169 true] [17592186335171 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335172 13194139535169 true] [17592186335171 1089 "q-106684" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335171 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535169 true] [17592186335171 1100 "Let $L$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant $0.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\n- The  zero-matrix $[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $L.$\n- For any $A\\in L,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in L$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$\n- For any $A,B,C\\in L,$ we have $(A+B)-C=A+(B-C).$" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335171 1113 #uuid "51c5420f-21df-52d3-9654-33ad4cc8c519" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335171 1145 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|=0.$ Hence, $[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\in L.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any matrix $A\\in L,$ there is a corresponding negative matrix $-A$ such that\n\n$$\nA+(-A)=A-A=O.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n|-A|=|-1\\cdot A|=(-1)^{2}\\cdot |A|=1\\cdot 0=0,\n$$\n\nhence $-A\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any matrices $A,B\\in L,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\n(A+B)-C=(A+B)+(-C)=A+(B+(-C))=A+(B-C).\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335173 13194139535169 true] [17592186335172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335174 13194139535169 true] [17592186335172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335175 13194139535169 true] [17592186335172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335176 13194139535169 true] [17592186335172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335177 13194139535169 true] [17592186335172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535169 true] [17592186335172 1041 "selection" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335172 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335173 13194139535169 true] [17592186335172 1110 #uuid "5ecc987c-c8cc-5f63-baef-e6473fad4fc5" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335173 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335173 1111 #uuid "b4f5a861-cd09-5c30-b707-42e1acd9252f" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335174 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335174 1111 #uuid "556a8812-7d1e-5303-95bb-888adfae35d3" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335175 1034 "III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335175 1111 #uuid "83361874-268d-5583-8d18-cd6e94b010bb" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335176 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335176 1111 #uuid "0097cb62-2f3d-509c-9f0d-1926f58b2818" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335177 1034 "II only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335177 1111 #uuid "e7f377a7-ebda-5213-8b57-4a75ebe9791b" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335178 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335179 13194139535169 true] [17592186335178 1089 "q-106810" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335178 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535169 true] [17592186335178 1100 "Let $J$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is at most $2.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\frac{1}{x}\\in J$\n- For any $p(x)\\in J,$ we have $1\\cdot p(x)\\in J$\n- For any $p(x),q(x)\\in J$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))=\\alpha p(x)-\\alpha q(x)$" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335178 1113 #uuid "2ed7ded9-5099-5079-b0d1-49a9bfed8737" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335178 1145 "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $J$ contains only polynomials whose degree is at most $2.$ However, $\\frac{1}{x}$ is *not* a polynomial. So, $\\frac{1}{x}\\notin J.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in J$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $p(x),q(x)\\in J,$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the results of $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))=\\alpha p(x)-\\alpha q(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335180 13194139535169 true] [17592186335179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335181 13194139535169 true] [17592186335179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335182 13194139535169 true] [17592186335179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335183 13194139535169 true] [17592186335179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335184 13194139535169 true] [17592186335179 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535169 true] [17592186335179 1041 "selection" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335179 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335181 13194139535169 true] [17592186335179 1110 #uuid "846eb4a8-6ca1-5379-97cd-39eb710b2fe0" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335180 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335180 1111 #uuid "65b19ade-b939-5d98-bb21-5b9723c5bd72" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335181 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335181 1111 #uuid "726d6301-05bb-596a-83b9-53ee99821c87" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335182 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335182 1111 #uuid "295d9428-3428-5375-b01e-a822afe2ec42" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335183 1034 "III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335183 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335183 1111 #uuid "8390585d-c10a-5162-8592-2302c83513c8" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335184 1034 "II only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335184 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335184 1111 #uuid "a92a2689-48ad-5fdf-bdca-8496635c8d00" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335185 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335186 13194139535169 true] [17592186335185 1089 "q-35663" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335185 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535169 true] [17592186335185 1100 "Let $S$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is greater than or equal to $2.$  Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $f(x)\\in S,$ where $f(x)=2x.$\n- For every $p(x),q(x)\\in S,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)\\in S.$\n- The set is closed under addition." 13194139535169 true] [17592186335185 1113 #uuid "75e40a9f-59c0-5201-b48c-eff45f525de1" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335185 1145 "Let's verify the statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $S$ contains only polynomials whose degree is greater than or equal to $2.$ However, \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡(2x)=1\\ne 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2x\\notin S.$\n\n- Statement II is false. There exist functions in $S$ such that their sum is *not* in $S.$ For example, let $p(x)=x+{x}^{2}$ and $q(x)=x-{x}^{2}.$ Notice that both these functions belong to $S$ since $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p(x))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡(q(x))=2\\ge 2.$ However,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p(x)+q(x))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡((x+{x}^{2})+(x-{x}^{2}))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡(2x)=1≱2.\n$$\n\nHence, $p(x)+q(x)\\notin S.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335187 13194139535169 true] [17592186335186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335188 13194139535169 true] [17592186335186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335189 13194139535169 true] [17592186335186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335190 13194139535169 true] [17592186335186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335191 13194139535169 true] [17592186335186 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535169 true] [17592186335186 1041 "selection" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335186 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335187 13194139535169 true] [17592186335186 1110 #uuid "de98d96e-99ba-5d51-ba85-c94fae413924" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335187 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335187 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335187 1111 #uuid "70383f63-9151-57a1-a1e1-f3be45c22395" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335188 1034 "I only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335188 1111 #uuid "251b7194-7a28-5ee9-bb47-ee7670b68ac4" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335189 1034 "III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335189 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335189 1111 #uuid "d0c0a7d9-5454-51ef-bdb9-737a03fee122" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335190 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335190 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335190 1111 #uuid "d183db47-6361-5823-9c56-2eb71ee80013" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335191 1034 "II only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335191 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335191 1111 #uuid "baad26ef-4978-5030-938c-8c508904b95a" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335192 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335193 13194139535169 true] [17592186335192 1089 "q-94661" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335192 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535169 true] [17592186335192 1100 "Let $F$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax+b,$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The zero-polynomial belongs to $F.$\n- For the zero polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have $p(x)+0=p(x).$\n- There are polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in F$ such that $p(x)+q(x)\\ne q(x)+p(x).$" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335192 1113 #uuid "fda9a634-4efe-5341-94d8-2c5e65931cee" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335192 1145 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the zero-polynomial can be represented as\n\n$$\n0=0\\cdot x+0.\n$$\n\nHence, $0\\in F.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for the zero-polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in F,$ we have\n\n$$\np(x)+0=p(x)\n$$\n\nsince $0$ is the unique zero element in the set of all polynomials.\n\n- Statement III is false. For any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in F,$ we have that\n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x)\n$$\n\nsince the addition of polynomials is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335194 13194139535169 true] [17592186335193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335195 13194139535169 true] [17592186335193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335196 13194139535169 true] [17592186335193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335197 13194139535169 true] [17592186335193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335198 13194139535169 true] [17592186335193 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535169 true] [17592186335193 1041 "selection" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335193 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335198 13194139535169 true] [17592186335193 1110 #uuid "dd86c685-8465-5157-aaf0-8520377a1003" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335194 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335194 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335194 1111 #uuid "6991c36b-2692-585c-ba1b-3fc0aee71d37" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335195 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335195 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335195 1111 #uuid "b8b7c65c-034d-5abe-a962-77e8c6ac308a" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335196 1034 "I only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335196 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335196 1111 #uuid "c1f59990-80a0-5d35-8269-d82e735c13ab" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335197 1034 "III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335197 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335197 1111 #uuid "51f0cd5a-84a0-51c1-96a8-ecea215abacb" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335198 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335198 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335198 1111 #uuid "88e05fa5-1b2a-50cd-8798-542e78e421e4" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335199 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335200 13194139535169 true] [17592186335199 1089 "q-94741" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335199 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535169 true] [17592186335199 1100 "Let $U$ be the set of functions of the form $p(x)=ax,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).$\n- Multiplication by $1$ does not change elements in $U.$\n- For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335199 1113 #uuid "6c197270-87fd-57d5-ae7b-88e7b887422c" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335199 1145 "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in U$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in U$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in U$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335201 13194139535169 true] [17592186335200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335202 13194139535169 true] [17592186335200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335203 13194139535169 true] [17592186335200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335204 13194139535169 true] [17592186335200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335205 13194139535169 true] [17592186335200 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535169 true] [17592186335200 1041 "selection" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335200 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335201 13194139535169 true] [17592186335200 1110 #uuid "e8f8637a-2371-53d5-8916-c8aed59d666f" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335201 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335201 1111 #uuid "653e87ae-801d-5f15-a2da-68480e0000dd" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335202 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335202 1111 #uuid "96b4f91e-307f-51ed-b3d7-8c686f38b24f" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335203 1034 "I only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335203 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335203 1111 #uuid "1ef0e988-de00-5774-ba47-d308ca3bf47d" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335204 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335204 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335204 1111 #uuid "9b5b89be-9c30-5654-ab40-bece9be05f85" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335205 1034 "II only" 13194139535169 true] [17592186335205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535169 true] [17592186335205 1111 #uuid "4a7dce09-da65-58c0-8608-8a2c0daaca68" 13194139535169 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-106684" 17592186335171 "q-106684/selection" 17592186335172 "q-106684/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" 17592186335173 "q-106684/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" 175921863